<emu-intro id="sec-intro">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>

  <p>The TEA API is created to support automation of the software supply chain. Upstream
    vendors and open source projects can use this standard to keep downstream consumers
    up to date with transparency artefacts such as, but not limited to, bill of materials,
    VEX files, attestations and much more.</p>

  <p>This specification defines a standard, format agnostic, API for the exchange of
    product related artefacts, like BOMs, between systems.</p>

  <p>The TEA Consumer API is a read-only interface for retrieving and validating transparency data.</p>

  <p>A TEA client needs to support TEA discovery using the TEI identifier,
    using DNS to find a set of TEA services. Discovery can be based on
    existing product identifiers instead of creating new ones.</p>

  <p>The API provides access to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Products and product releases</li>
    <li>Components and component releases</li>
    <li>Collections</li>
    <li>Artefacts</li>
    <li>Common Lifecycle Events documents (CLE)</li>
    <li>Compliance-document identifiers and related metadata</li>
  </ul>

  <p>The TEA Consumer API is broader than a simple product/component lookup API. It covers release history, collections, artefacts,
    lifecycle data, discovery, and compliance-document-aware identifiers.</p>
</emu-intro>
